abstract: >-
  An R package that simulates and compares network robustness to random
  node failures and targeted attacks, extending the approach of Albert,
  Jeong & Barabási (2000) and generalising the R-index of Schneider et al.
  (2011) to any network indicator. Includes node removal, edge removal,
  isolated knock-out and Shapley-value node importance, with a Monte Carlo
  null-model framework for testing whether an attack is significantly more
  damaging than random failure.
